{"availability":"available","full":"baseballyama/svelte-shaker","name":"svelte-shaker","description":"Build-time dead code elimination for Svelte 5 via whole program partial evaluation. ","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":25,"forks":2,"created":"2024-05-24T14:18:12Z","updated":"2026-10-16T02:49:14Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://baseballyama.github.io/svelte-shaker/","topics":["svelte","tree-shaking"],"demo":"https://baseballyama.github.io/svelte-shaker/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T13:25:17.065Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T13:25:17.065Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T13:25:17.065Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T00:25:33.116Z","stars":25,"forks":2},{"at":"2026-10-16T13:25:17.065Z","stars":25,"forks":2}],"technologies":["Svelte"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A sound, source-level tree-shaker for Svelte 5 (runes) components.","▶ Try it in the browser: — the playground runs the engine entirely client-side.","svelte-shaker runs in your production build, before the Svelte compiler, and slims each .svelte file by partially evaluating it against how your whole app actually uses it: props no call site passes (or that always receive the same value) are folded to their constant, the dead {#if} arms behind them are deleted, the props are dropped from $props(), the attributes are removed at every call site, and rules whose class can never be produced are stripped."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/baseballyama/svelte-shaker/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"064c4fee224c234cf4ee4675d731900763d441d199c36fb4da5392fdd054f00b","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T00:25:33.220Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T13:25:17.226Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A sound, source-level tree-shaker for Svelte 5 (runes) components.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/baseballyama/svelte-shaker/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"0